/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Prism.PentagonalPrism.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 48`, `matAt x 39` and `(x 57, x 58)` are a weak fit of `Prism.PentagonalPrism.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem prismPentagonalPrism_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Prism.PentagonalPrism.polyhedron Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.S N 48 39 57 := by
  rw [Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.len_eq Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.theta_spec Nieuwland.Polyhedra.PrismPentagonalPrismDim.root) Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.par_ok Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.zs_eq Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.weak_ok Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.poly_eq Pose.PrismPentagonalPrism.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
